dd-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Voltage and current module","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=756/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd756.htm","s":"BIM-05-1","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"EGT and head temperature module","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=758/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd758.htm","s":"BIM-12-2","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Wideband air/fuel module","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=785/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd785.htm","s":"BIM-13-2","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Clock module","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=759/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd759.htm","s":"BIM-16-1","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Compass with outside temperature","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=760/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd760.htm","s":"BIM-17-2","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Quad air pressure module","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=761/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd761.htm","s":"BIM-19-2","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Part","t":"Tire pressure monitoring (TPMS)","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1108/category_id=646/mode=prod/prd1108.htm","s":"BIM-22-3","x":"efi bim module expansion add-on"},{"k":"Help","t":"How can I pay for my Dakota Digital order?","u":"faq.html#q1","s":"Purchasing","x":"We accept Visa, Mastercard, Amex or Discover. If you do not have a credit card, you can call us and we will give you the total with shipping that you can mail in to us. Unfortunately Dakota Digital do"},{"k":"Help","t":"I don't see a kit for my vehicle. Can I still have Dakota Digital gauges?","u":"faq.html#q2","s":"Purchasing","x":"Most vehicles that we don't have a kit for can be handled by our custom shop. For most customs you will need to send in your original bezel and gauge housing so that we can remove the factory gauges a"},{"k":"Help","t":"I ordered a motorcycle gauge from a dealer but I don't have the speed adaptor that's mentioned in the instructions. Why didn't I get one?","u":"faq.html#q3","s":"Purchasing","x":"The speed adaptors are a separate item that you need to order along with your gauge. They are not included, so that our dealers can stock one main unit and a few speed adaptors and have it work on man"},{"k":"Help","t":"Are your digital and/or analog gauges reliable? Is there a warranty?","u":"faq.html#q4","s":"Durability and warranty","x":"Yes Dakota Digital gauges are reliable. Dakota Digital has been in business since 1986 and we have tens of thousands of units on the road. Over the years we have continued to improve our products with"},{"k":"Help","t":"Will it wreck your gauges if my bike is in the rain?","u":"faq.html#q5","s":"Durability and warranty","x":"No. All Dakota Digital motorcycle gauges are designed to survive in the weather. The circuit boards are all internally coated for weather resistance so even if water gets into the housing they will no"},{"k":"Help","t":"My bike vibrates like crazy! Can Dakota Digital gauges take vibration?","u":"faq.html#q6","s":"Durability and warranty","x":"Yes they can take it! Our gauges were designed with custom cycles in mind so they are beefed up internally to take the abuse that a big stroker motor puts out. Dakota Digital motorcycle gauges use mac"},{"k":"Help","t":"The Dakota Digital technician told me that I'd need to send my unit in for repair. Where do I send it and what do I include?","u":"faq.html#q7","s":"Repairs","x":"Send items that need repair to: Dakota Digital Inc., Attn: Repair Dept., 4510 W. 61st St North, Sioux Falls SD 57107. Be sure to include the complete unit to be repaired as well as your name, address,"},{"k":"Help","t":"How much will it cost to repair my unit?","u":"faq.html#q8","s":"Repairs","x":"That will depend on the cause of the problem, which product, and if the unit is still covered under warranty. Typical non-warranty repairs start at $65. If the repair is covered under warranty there w"},{"k":"Help","t":"I have a vehicle with factory digital gauges but they don't work. Can Dakota Digital repair them?","u":"faq.html#q9","s":"Repairs","x":"Unfortunately Dakota Digital can not repair OEM digital gauges. You will likely need to have them repaired or replaced by the manufacturer. However, we may be able to build you a custom set of Dakota "},{"k":"Help","t":"Can I install the gauges myself?","u":"faq.html#q10","s":"Installation","x":"Several of our customers install their gauges themselves, although depending upon your comfort level, skill and experience, it may be worth seeking out a qualified installer."},{"k":"Help","t":"I have an older bike with a cable driven speedo. Can I use your speedometer?","u":"faq.html#q11","s":"Installation","x":"Dakota Digital gauges can be used on cable drive or electronic speedo applications. Just be sure to order the appropriate speed adaptor for your application when you place the order. Our gauges can al"},{"k":"Help","t":"Can I get a red digital display?","u":"faq.html#q12","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"This will depend on the item you are ordering. On automotive full gauge systems (items with part numbers starting \"VFD and RET\") you can get a red display as a custom color for an additional charge. H"},{"k":"Help","t":"Will I be able to see the automotive digital gauges during the day?","u":"faq.html#q13","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"As long as you stick to the standard colors (blue or teal) daylight visibility is very good. For the best visibility we recommend the teal display. The teal is recommended for convertible applications"},{"k":"Help","t":"How is visibility during the day and at night on my motorcycle?","u":"faq.html#q14","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"Night time visibility on all Dakota Digital gauges will be excellent. Daytime visibility will depend on the application. The MLX series of direct-plug in Harley Davidson instruments use high-visibilit"},{"k":"Help","t":"In the picture of the gauges that I want the fuel gauge reads 99. What does this mean?","u":"faq.html#q15","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"The fuel gauge reads as a percentage. 99 would mean that the tank is 99% full, 25 would mean that you have a quarter tank (25%)."},{"k":"Help","t":"I have higher gears than stock. Will the speedometer be accurate?","u":"faq.html#q16","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"Dakota Digital speedometers can be calibrated for nearly any tire/gearing combination. Once the gauges are installed you will calibrate them for your combination using a simple push button calibration"},{"k":"Help","t":"How high will the Dakota Digital speedometer go up to?","u":"faq.html#q17","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"Dakota Digital speedometers can read up to 199 or 255MPH (KPH) depending upon the model. VHX, HDX, RTX and GRFX instrument systems will read up to 120/140/160MPH and up to 255MPH displayed in the digi"},{"k":"Help","t":"I am using Dakota Digital gauges and plan to disconnect my battery while storing the vehicle over the winter. Will I lose my odometer reading and settings?","u":"faq.html#q18","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"Your odometer reading and settings will be saved in hard memory so disconnecting the battery will not affect anything. Make sure your battery is fully charged when re-starting in the spring."},{"k":"Help","t":"Is it possible to put my vehicle's odometer reading on the Dakota Digital gauges or do I have to start at zero miles? I looked at the installation instructions but could not find how to set the odometer.","u":"faq.html#q19","s":"Gauge readings and display","x":"Dakota Digital gauges come from the factory at zero miles unless you specify that you want the odometer set. Dakota Digital can set the odometer on our digital gauges to a specific mileage reading. It"},{"k":"Build","t":"Big Oak 1961 Impala","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1363/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1363.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"BBT Fabrications 1969 Firebird","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1362/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1362.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Rodney Kline 1955 Chevy","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1361/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1361.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Nichols Fab 1932 Ford Truck","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1353/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1353.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Estrada 1956 Chevy 3100","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1350/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1350.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Weaver Customs 75 Jeep Wagoneer","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1347/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1347.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Goodguys Columbus 2022","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1346/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1346.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Scott's Hotrods 'n Customs K5 Blazer","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1345/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1345.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"Evans Sweet Patina 1957 Chevy","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1344/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1344.htm","s":"Feature build","x":""},{"k":"Build","t":"ASC Bronco 'Ol Blue","u":"https://www.dakotadigital.com/index.cfm/page/ptype=product/product_id=1342/category_id=643/mode=prod/prd1342.htm"